  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and clients pay for useful skills and reliability. They judge you by proof, not by the story you tell about your choice.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is testing a belief with one small fact.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and myths about choosing a career: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can summarise options and draft questions. Routine research shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, honest self-knowledge and accountability for choices hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to gather facts and check them; later, own the decision.
  </p>

